WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
The final topic we'll cover is infant choking. We know that babies are naturally

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.040
curious. They explore the world with their mouths, which means if an object

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.880
fits in their hand, it will likely end up in their mouth eventually. Your first

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.559
step is to assess the situation. A very helpful rule to remember is that a

00:00:19.559 --> 00:00:24.840
crying baby is a breathing baby. If the choking is mild, you can simply lean the

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.559
infant forward and pat them on the back to help them clear it. However, if the

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:34.320
choking is severe, meaning the baby is unable to cry or breathe, you must act

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.160
immediately using the five and five technique. For the best stability, it is

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.119
recommended to sit down with your feet flat on the floor and your legs in a V

00:00:43.119 --> 00:00:47.480
shape to help support the infant's weight. Place the infant face down on

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.880
your forearm, using your hand to support their head and ensure their head is

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.200
positioned lower than their chest. Deliver five firm back thrusts between

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.279
the shoulder blades while keeping the baby tilted downward. If the object

00:01:00.279 --> 00:01:04.400
doesn't clear, flip the baby over onto your other forearm and deliver five

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.400
chest thrusts. Continue alternating between five back thrusts and five chest

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.779
thrusts until the object is ejected or the baby becomes unresponsive. If the

00:01:14.779 --> 00:01:20.239
infant loses consciousness, you must transition immediately to CPR. Important,

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:25.879
regardless of age, if a choking victim becomes unresponsive, begin CPR as you

00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:30.639
learn today. The only adjustment is every time you open the airway to

00:01:30.639 --> 00:01:35.739
deliver rescue breaths, look inside the mouth. Only remove the obstruction if you

00:01:35.739 --> 00:01:41.000
can clearly see it. Never perform a blind finger sweep as this can accidentally

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:47.680
push the object deeper into the airway. Now, please find a chair and take a seat

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.279
with your infant mannequin. We're going to practice the five and five technique

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:57.320
together. Remember to place the infant face down along your forearm. Use your

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.879
hand to support their jaw and head, but be very careful not to cover their face

00:02:01.879 --> 00:02:06.879
or mouth. Rest your forearm on your thigh and tilt the baby so their head is lower

00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:11.639
than their chest. Perform five firm back blows right between the shoulder blades

00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:15.919
using the heel of your hand, then flip the baby by supporting the back of the

00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:20.639
baby's head, sandwiching them between your arms, and then turn them over onto

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:27.199
your other leg. Again, keep that head tilted down. Now, deliver five quick chest

00:02:27.199 --> 00:02:32.320
thrusts in the center of the chest. Keep cycling through five back blows, then

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:35.479
five chest thrusts.

